t verified at [A, A+m); unaligned remainder (length ≥ 25) is aligned elsewhere by seed voting with count>=2 and verified. Implement generically:\n\n```python\ndef split_candidates_from_clusters(...)\n```\nKeep it manageable: primary = 2-cluster reads. Secondary = partial-match reads: take unaligned portion (prefix before match or suffix after match — determined by where matches occur; from verification mismatch pattern compute match prefix length and suffix length: longest prefix with <=1 mismatch per 20bp window... simpler: per-position mismatch array; find longest good prefix and suffix). For secondary reads: good prefix length gpre, good suffix length gsuf, middle bad. If gpre >= 30 and gsuf >= 30: prefix diag = d1 (from cluster), then search suffix elsewhere: seed vote on suffix segment alone with offsets; find best cluster with count>=2, verify. Symmetric for the case prefix is missing.\n\nThis is getting long but let me implement carefully. Realistically, at 2x coverage we expect ~2 junction reads per breakpoint (both ends) → ~4 split reads total, of which maybe 2-3 are discoverable. Discordant pairs: ~1-2. Depth carries the main signal.\n\nDepth-based edge estimation for fallback: from the 10kb profile, left edge = boundary where ratio drops; define depth_left_edge = first low 10kb bin start position (0-based), depth_right_edge = last low bin end position. These bracket true breakpoints within ~10kb + noise.\n\nIntegration:\n- Use split-read breakpoints if available (median across reads).\n- Else, if discordant: left = max(start1)+READ_LEN (lower bound), right = min(start2) (upper bound).\n- Else, depth edge.\nThen round.\n\nOK, also main() should write outputs. Also record timing.\n\nNow let me write the chunks. Also double-check kmer_codes loop: km = codes[:n].astype(uint64); then for j in 1..k-1: km = (km<<2)|codes[j:j+n]. At the end, km[i] = code of kmer i with first base as most-significant bit. Mask invalid kmers with sentinel (1<<63). Since valid kmers