< ref_len guaranteed (candidates are valid ≤ ref_len − L; starts of mapped reads are valid ✓).\n\nwrite_outputs: uses ctx[\"matches1\"] etc. — main returns via write_outputs(locals()) — locals() contains matches1, starts1, mq1, mq2, n_n, ref_name, mappable, ratio_in, supporting, bp_method, bp_note… let me verify all keys accessed in write_outputs/build_report exist in main's locals at the time of call:\n- ref_len ✓, n_pairs ✓, n_map1 ✓, n_map2 ✓, start_r ✓ end_r ✓ size_r ✓ pos1 ✓ end1 ✓, depth ✓ interval ✓ pa ✓ disc_clusters ✓ splits ✓ b0,b1 ✓ (from interval unpack) — wait, b0,b1 are defined in main ✓, coarse ✓ defined in main (coarse = depth[\"coarse\"]) ✓, mq1 ✓ mq2 ✓, n_n ✓ ref_name ✓ mappable ✓ (from depth_analysis) ✓ matches1/2 ✓ starts1/2 ✓ ratio_in ✓ supporting ✓ bp_method ✓ bp_note ✓.\n\nIn build_report: qc fields — seg['depleted_coarse_bins'] is a list [b0,b1] ✓; ins['discordant_clusters'] is a list of dicts with int values ✓ JSON-serializable; in the report loop over discordant clusters, c['left_lower_bound'] etc. ✓.\n\nJSON: disc_clusters dicts contain pair_ids list ✓.\n\nsplits dict values: end(str), read_id(int), strand(int), J_left int, J_right int, split int, pre/suf int, size_on_ref int ✓.\n\nOK, fixes:\n1. Remove rcc parameter from split_from_partials signature.\n2. Fix s_hi in find_split_reads.\n3. Replace the dead code block in split_from_partials with the suffix-explained guard.\n\nLet me apply these in Python's file editing.\n"}}
