s=b-a, median_ratio=float(np.nanmedian(ratio[a:b])), frac_kmer_multiplicity=frac_mult, split_reads_supporting=int(n_split), discordant_pairs_spanning=int(sel.sum()), called_deletion=False))\n    return out\n```\nNote: interval_bins_mask = np.zeros(n_bins,bool); mask[b0:b1]=True.\n\nAlso, should we flag high-ratio bins (duplications with piled-up reads) for the report? Optional; mention it generally in the report. Keep the audit to dips only, but also compute a list of high-ratio bins (ratio>1.8) for qc (briefly).\n\nNew version of write_outputs(ctx): build qc dict:\n\n- inputs, alignment, coverage, insert_size,\n- depth_segmentation: coarse bin, median ratio, depleted coarse bins [b0,b1], inner ratio, zygosity, fine edges.\n- breakpoints: raw (left_raw 0-based = pos1 = last retained base? note) — store: raw_breakpoint_left_1based = pos1 (= left_raw), raw_breakpoint_right_1based = end1 (= right_raw) (last retained / last deleted), raw_size = end1-pos1, method, note; split reads supporting the interval (list); spanning pairs list; depth edges; rounding result; precision note.\n- artifact_audit: dip_audit list + description.\n- deletion: final.\n\nbuild_report: summary table, data, methods, evidence (depth bins, exact split reads with match counts, spanning pairs with coordinates), \"evidence vs precision\" section, artifact/paralogy section (secondary dips explained by segmental duplication; no junction evidence; deterministic tie-break), output files.\n\nAlso, for the split reads in the report: pre/suf match counts and positions.\n\nNow let's write the chunk."}}
